.TH KRYX\-SRC 8 "November 2026" "kryx-linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kryx\-src \- unified CRUX/KryX source build, linting, and release\-staging machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kryx\-src
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ...\& ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kryx\-src
is a standalone static Go source\-building and release\-staging companion to
.BR pe (8),
inspired by Void Linux's
.BR xbps\-src .
It shares
.BR pe 's
internal Pkgfile parser, builder, package database, and repository indexer while
adding a canonical port registry that resolves ports uniformly by directory path,
basename, declared
.B Pkgfile
.BR name= ,
or collection prefix, across both multi\-collection trees and single\-port repositories.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pkg \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fItarget\fR ... \fR(alias: \fBbuild\fR)
Expand
.I target
arguments (port path, basename, package name, collection name, or
.BR all ),
optionally resolve recursive dependencies in topological order
.RB ( \-\-deps ),
satisfy uninstalled dependencies binary\-first from
.I index.json
(or from source with
.BR \-\-source\-deps ),
and compile target archives into
.IR \-\-out\-dir .
.TP
.B lint \fR[\fB\-\-ports \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fItarget\fR ...] \fR(alias: \fBcheck\fR)
Validate
.B Pkgfile
recipes across a ports tree, detecting missing required fields, directory\-vs\-name
mismatches, duplicate package names within a collection, missing dependency targets,
and dependency cycles.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-ports \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fItarget\fR ...] \fR(alias: \fBls\fR)
List discovered ports with their relative directory path, package name (when it
differs from the directory basename), and full version.
.TP
.B stage \fR[\fIoptions\fR] \fR(alias: \fBindex\fR)
Scan
.I \-\-packages
for CRUX
.I .pkg.tar.<ext>
archives, enrich metadata from
.IR \-\-ports ,
merge into
.IR \-\-index ,
and optionally copy archives into
.I \-\-upload\-dir
with GitHub\-Releases\-safe filenames
.RB ( #
replaced by
.BR . ).
.TP
.B rewrite\-urls \-\-index \fIpath\fR \-\-assets\-json \fIfile\fR \fR[\fB\-\-packages \fIdir\fR]
Update download URLs in
.I index.json
using the JSON payload returned by
.B gh release view \-\-json assets
and verify that every built archive resolves to an uploaded asset URL.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
kryx\-src lint \-\-ports /usr/ports
kryx\-src pkg \-\-ports ./ports \-\-work\-root /tmp/work \-\-out\-dir ./dist/packages \-\-deps \-\-force linux\-6.18
kryx\-src stage \-\-packages ./dist/packages \-\-ports ./ports \-\-index ./stage/index.json \-\-upload\-dir ./stage/upload
kryx\-src rewrite\-urls \-\-index ./stage/index.json \-\-assets\-json ./stage/assets.json \-\-packages ./dist/packages
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pe (8),
.BR pe\-index (8),
.BR gports (8)
